# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored (`.env*` with an `!.env.example`
# exception) — do not commit real credentials.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL — interim content database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# See documentation/technical-specification/BLOCKERS.md §5. This database holds
# CONTENT ONLY (tours, destinations, group departures, brochure metadata). It
# holds NO LEADS and has NO admin UI.
#
# LEAVING THIS UNSET IS A SUPPORTED MODE, not a broken one. The composition root
# (src/content/content-adapter.ts) falls back to FixtureContentAdapter when
# DATABASE_URL is absent, so the site builds and runs with no database at all —
# which is how the test suite, `npm run build` and the Playwright suite run today.
#
# Local development with the docker-compose `db` service:
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://gty:gty_local_dev_password@localhost:5432/gty_content?schema=public"
#
# Deployed (Railway): the same Postgres INSTANCE as the CRM, but its own database
# /schema and its own credentials. It is NOT the CRM's database — never point this
# at the CRM's tables.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>:<port>/<database>?schema=gty_site_content"
